  "body": "### Project Website\n\nhttps://quven.tv/\n\n### Describe what data should be consumed by Homarr\n\nHi!\n\nWould it be possible to add Quven as a supported integration in Homarr?\n\nQuven is a self-hosted media server, similar to Plex and Jellyfin, and I think it would fit really well into Homarr's ecosystem.\n\nIt would be great to have a Quven integration/widget allowing users to display information such as:\n\nServer status\nNumber of active users/sessions\nCurrently playing media\nServer/library statistics\nPossibly other information available through the Quven API\n\nEven a basic integration showing the server status and active sessions would already be really useful.\n\nQuven is still relatively new, but it is actively being developed, and I think supporting it early would be a great addition for users building self-hosted media server setups.\n\nI\u2019d be happy to help with testing the integration on a real Quven server if needed.\n\nThanks! \u2764\ufe0f\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_\n\n### Public API available?\n\nYes, available on a website\n\n### Are you willing to contribute this yourself?\n\nYes",
